smtprelay, the fetch job, and Dovecot all log to the mail facility,
so their lines land interleaved in /var/log/maillog, and nothing says
so. Following one service there means filtering by tag by hand. A
successful fetch logged nothing at all, so the log could not show
that mail had arrived.

Each service now has its own file under /var/log/lab-mail/, rotated
like maillog, which still gets everything. The fetch job reports how
many messages each pull brought and names mbsync's exit status when
it fails.

syslogd in the jail opens no network socket. lab-mail shares
beastie's addresses, so a socket would contend for UDP port 514 with
every other jail's syslogd, and nothing needs remote logging here.
